## Approach

Replace the hand-rolled `louvain()` with a thin wrapper around `leiden-rs`. The crate uses dense `0..n` usize indices, so the wrapper maps our `i64` node IDs ↔ usize indices (same pattern the current `louvain()` already does). Rename `LouvainResult` → `ClusterResult` since the algorithm changes. Keep `auto_tune()` structure but switch it to call `leiden()`. Use a fixed seed (42) for determinism — leiden-rs supports `seed(u64)` via `StdRng`. Start with `Modularity` quality function (matches current behavior); evaluate `CPM` as part of the spike's comparison run.

